  url: 'https://www.mindvalley.com/entrepreneur-collection',
  body: "I want to share three stories with you today.\n\nEach person started exactly where you are — in Everyday Bliss, learning to manage their stress, finding their calm, building inner resilience. And each one upgraded to the full Entrepreneurship & AI Collection.\n\nWhat happened next is worth your attention.\n\n---\n\n**ELENA, 39, MIAMI, FL** — \"I thought my stress was caused by my business. It was the other way around. My stress was causing my business problems.\"\n\nElena runs a boutique digital marketing agency with 6 employees. She bought Everyday Bliss because she was having panic attacks. \"I'd wake up at 4 AM, heart pounding, mind racing through every worst-case scenario. Client calls made me nauseous. I was running a successful business and I was miserable.\"\n\nPaul McKenna's techniques started working within the first two weeks. \"The panic attacks stopped. Not reduced — stopped. I felt like a different person. But then I noticed something unexpected: my business decisions started getting better.\"\n\nWhen she upgraded to the collection, she combined Everyday Bliss with Money EQ and Amplify with AI. \"Ken Honda showed me that my panic wasn't about the business — it was about money. Specifically, about my fear that the money would disappear. Once I healed that, the panic lost its fuel.\"\n\nThen she applied AI. \"With a calm nervous system and a healed money story, I could finally think strategically. I used Amplify with AI to automate our reporting, content creation, and client onboarding. Three months of implementation freed up 15 hours a week.\"\n\n**Result: Elena's agency revenue grew from $720,000 to $1.3 million in 14 months. She works 35 hours a week instead of 55. Her team reports she's \"a completely different leader.\"** The panic attacks never returned.\n\n---\n\n**THOMAS, 45, SEATTLE, WA** — \"I was the calmest underachiever you'd ever meet. Everyday Bliss gave me peace. The collection gave me ambition I could actually sustain.\"\n\nThomas is a financial planner with his own practice. He bought Everyday Bliss after a health scare — his doctor told him his cortisol levels were dangerously high. \"I needed to calm down or my body was going to force the issue.\"\n\nEveryday Bliss worked. His cortisol dropped. His sleep improved. His doctor was impressed.\n\nBut something unexpected happened. \"I got so good at being calm that I lost my edge. My practice was coasting. I wasn't growing. I'd found peace but lost my drive.\"\n\nThe collection changed the dynamic. \"Superbrain reignited my learning. I was absorbing new financial planning strategies, tax code changes, and client management techniques faster than ever — but without the frantic energy that used to fuel my learning. It was calm ambition. Focused ambition.\"\n\nBecoming Focused and Indistractable helped him restructure his days. \"I went from being available to everyone all the time to having protected deep work blocks where I built systems for my practice. That single change was worth the entire collection.\"\n\n**Result: Thomas's practice grew by 41% in one year — the first real growth in three years — while his cortisol stayed in the healthy range.** He calls it \"sustainable ambition.\" \"For the first time in my career, growth and health aren't in competition.\"\n\n---\n\n**ANGELA, 31, BROOKLYN, NY** — \"I didn't know that my relationship with money was a stress response. When I healed both at the same time, my entire business shifted.\"\n\nAngela is a freelance UX researcher who works with tech startups. She bought Everyday Bliss because she was burnt out. \"I'd been freelancing for 5 years and I was exhausted. Not physically — emotionally. Every project felt heavy. Every invoice felt like a confrontation.\"\n\nEveryday Bliss helped with the emotional weight. \"Paul's techniques taught me to process the accumulated stress instead of just pushing through it. I felt lighter. My work quality improved because I wasn't creating from a place of depletion.\"\n\nBut the invoicing problem persisted. \"I'd still feel sick sending invoices. I'd let clients pay late without saying anything. I'd accept lower rates to avoid the discomfort of negotiation.\"\n\nMoney EQ from the collection addressed this directly. \"Ken Honda helped me see that my discomfort with money was a specific wound — my family treated money discussions as taboo, almost shameful. I'd internalized the belief that asking for money was aggressive.\"\n\nThe combination of Everyday Bliss (processing the emotional stress) and Money EQ (healing the money belief) created a cascade. \"For the first time, I raised my rates with zero anxiety. Not just intellectually believing I was worth more, but *feeling* it in my body.\"\n\nShe then added Amplify with AI to systemize her research processes. \"I automated my survey analysis, report generation, and client presentation creation. Projects that took three weeks now take one.\"\n\n**Result: Angela's monthly income went from $6,200 to $14,800 in 8 months. She works with fewer clients but at premium rates.** She no longer feels sick when she sends invoices. \"That alone was worth a hundred times the collection price.\"\n\n---\n\nThree entrepreneurs. Three different manifestations of the same pattern.\n\n**Inner peace is the foundation. But the foundation needs walls, a roof, and a door that opens to the world.**\n\nYou've built the foundation with Everyday Bliss. The collection builds everything else.\n\n[Join Them →](https://www.mindvalley.com/entrepreneur-collection)\n\nTo your peaceful success,\n\n[Signature]\n\nP.S. Tomorrow: the math. Dollar for dollar, program for program, I'll show you exactly why this collection is the highest-ROI investment available to an entrepreneur right now. If numbers speak to you louder than stories, that email is for you."
